    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p>Hobgoblins embody the primal drive to grow and expand, and they satisfy it by forcing the world to bend to their will. Alone, a hobgoblin claims a stretch of woodland and pillages the wilds; together, hobgoblins build strict military hierarchies devoted to conquering lands and draining them of resources. They often enslave animals, monsters, and destructive Fey—goblins and bugbears above all—and may ally with dragons, warlords, servants of war gods, or any power that promises them new territory. Once a whole land is subdued, they look for the next conquest, across the seas, into the Underdark, or toward the stars and other planes. Hobgoblin warlords lead armies of hobgoblins and their allies, relying on experience and strategic thinking to direct them through the shifting tides of battle.</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
